CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ write through reference argument: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The constant evaluator does not model the write through the reference and
declines; the variable is then initialized at run time, with the same value.
